## Appendix B Engineering Acceptance, Resources, and Reproduction

### B.1 Training and Memory

Pure step processing across the 15 independent 7B runs totals 2.306 hours, with peak reserved memory of 24.547 GB. The original 15-run 9B experiment totals 3.919 hours and peaks at 21.104 GB. The six new factorial runs total approximately 2.36 hours and peak at 21.534 GB. These are PyTorch reserved-memory measurements, not whole-device `nvidia-smi` usage. The original complete 7B preflight on the 4090 reserves 24.43 GB, exceeding the then-fixed 22 GB admission limit. Formal independent training consequently runs on the 5090 after migration. The formal 24.547 GB peak is distinct from the preflight measurement.

The maximum pre-clipping gradient norm in the original 9B experiment is 768.76, with clipping at 1.0. Finite losses and gradients do not imply absence of spikes. BF16 checks, weight hashes, recovery states, and logs are retained. Historical whole-device memory traces are missing for old Stage C. Missing measurements are not filled with zero, and later samples are not substituted for historical peaks.

![Figure B1. Loss curves for the 15 independent 7B runs.](../results/protocol-v2-20261016/route-b-formal-loss-curves.png)

![Figure B2. Loss curves for the original 15 9B runs.](../results/protocol-v2-20261016/9b-training-final/loss-curves.png)

![Figure B3. Training curves for the factorial conditions.](../results/protocol-v2-20261016/9b-repair-final/report/loss-curves.png)

### B.2 Cost Accounting

At the user-specified rate of CNY 2.70/hour, pure step processing and generation in the original independent 7B experiment correspond to approximately CNY 48.89, excluding grounding reassessment. Original 9B pure training steps correspond to approximately CNY 10.58. Formal 9B evaluation and delivery take 26.417 wall-clock hours, corresponding to approximately CNY 71.33. These quantities use different scopes and cannot simply be combined with overlapping stages into an account total. The factorial budget cap is six training hours plus 24 evaluation hours, nominally CNY 81, but both phases finish early. Teacher API fees, loading, uploading, waiting, and historical debugging must be accounted for from actual usage; no total project bill is fabricated without complete billing evidence.

