## Appendix C Outstanding Original ARP Requirements and Submission Preparation

Exact-checkpoint API/local bridging, valid new audits and a formal revised C decision, independent two-reviewer grounding review, and budget interventions following an independent C-based choice remain incomplete. Commercial aliases such as `qwen3-vl-plus` cannot replace exact Qwen2.5-VL parameter nodes. The required per-axis bridge difference below 0.5 percentage points is not automatically satisfied by the present engineering success. Fixing A1/A2/U in the independent experiment does not validate the causal chain from scoring scale to axis selection.

Before submission, the authors should supply accurate names and affiliations, check dataset licenses and reproduction commands, verify bibliography metadata, and adapt the manuscript to the selected venue's format. Within its present evidence scope, the study can be framed as exploratory empirical research. Broader claims about a general mechanism or a cross-model method would require newly registered experiments with more seeds, additional model families, and representation-length controls. These boundaries remain explicit without preventing transparent reporting of the completed experiments.
